/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 2 Chronicles chapters 6-10
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("2chronicles", [
{n:6, name:"Solomon's Dedication Prayer", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 6:21",verse:"Hearken therefore unto the supplications of thy servant, and of thy people Israel, which they shall make toward this place: hear thou from thy dwelling place, even from heaven; and when thou hearest, forgive."}, facts:["Did you know Solomon prayed kneeling on a brasen scaffold five cubits long, five broad, and three high, set in the middle of the court where all Israel could see him?","Did you know Solomon's prayer covers war, drought, famine, plague, and even a stranger from a far country, making it one of the longest recorded prayers in Scripture?","Did you know that after building the grandest temple ever made, Solomon confessed that even the heaven of heavens cannot contain God?"], questions:[
{q:"How did Solomon describe the place where God had said He would dwell?", options:["The thick darkness","A house of cedar","The holy mountain","The city of David"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:1",verse:"Then said Solomon, The LORD hath said that he would dwell in the thick darkness.", insight:"Solomon began his prayer remembering that God dwells in thick darkness, a reminder that the temple was for God's glory, not for housing God."},
{q:"What did Solomon call the house he had built for the LORD?", options:["A house of habitation, and a place for His dwelling for ever","A house of sacrifice for burnt offerings","A house of rest for the ark only","A house of prayer for all the tribes"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:2",verse:"But I have built an house of habitation for thee, and a place for thy dwelling for ever.", insight:"He called it a dwelling place for ever, speaking in faith that God's presence would rest there for generations to come."},
{q:"What did Solomon stand and kneel upon when he prayed before all Israel?", options:["A brasen scaffold set in the midst of the court","The altar of burnt offering","A throne of ivory and gold","The steps of the porch"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:13",verse:"For Solomon had made a brasen scaffold, of five cubits long, and five cubits broad, and three cubits high, and had set it in the midst of the court: and upon it he stood, and kneeled down upon his knees before all the congregation of Israel, and spread forth his hands toward heaven,", insight:"The richest king in the world prayed from a bronze platform in the middle of the court, where every eye could see him humble himself."},
{q:"How large was the brasen scaffold Solomon had made?", options:["Five cubits long, five cubits broad, and three cubits high","Ten cubits long and five cubits high","Seven cubits round and two cubits high","Three cubits long, three broad, and one high"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:13",verse:"For Solomon had made a brasen scaffold, of five cubits long, and five cubits broad, and three cubits high, and had set it in the midst of the court: and upon it he stood, and kneeled down upon his knees before all the congregation of Israel, and spread forth his hands toward heaven,", insight:"Even the platform he knelt on was measured and ordered, showing the care Israel took with everything that touched worship."},
{q:"What did Solomon declare about God at the start of his prayer?", options:["There is no God like Thee in heaven nor in earth","Thou art the God of Israel only","No king is greater than Thee","Thou dwellest in the house I built"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:14",verse:"And said, O LORD God of Israel, there is no God like thee in the heaven, nor in the earth; which keepest covenant, and shewest mercy unto thy servants, that walk before thee with all their hearts:", insight:"Before asking anything, Solomon worshipped. Praise first, requests second, is the pattern of a heart that knows who God is."},
{q:"What promise to David did Solomon ask God to keep?", options:["That David would never lack a man to sit on the throne of Israel","That David's house would be rebuilt in gold","That David's enemies would be destroyed","That David's name would be carved on the temple"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:16",verse:"Now therefore, O LORD God of Israel, keep with thy servant David my father that which thou hast promised him, saying, There shall not fail thee a man in my sight to sit upon the throne of Israel; yet so that thy children take heed to their way to walk in my law, as thou hast walked before me.", insight:"Solomon anchored his prayer in God's covenant promise to David, reminding us to pray God's own words back to Him."},
{q:"What did Solomon admit about the temple in his prayer?", options:["Not even the heaven of heavens can contain God, much less this house","The temple was greater than any house on earth","God would never leave the temple","The temple made God near to Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:18",verse:"But will God in very deed dwell with men on the earth? behold, heaven and the heaven of heavens cannot contain thee; how much less this house which I have built!", insight:"The builder of the grandest temple ever made confessed it could not hold God. Big faith never confuses the building with the One it honors."},
{q:"What did Solomon ask God to keep upon the temple day and night?", options:["His eyes","His hand of judgment","His cloud by day","His fire by night"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:20",verse:"That thine eyes may be open upon this house day and night, upon the place whereof thou hast said that thou wouldest put thy name there; to hearken unto the prayer which thy servant prayeth toward this place.", insight:"Solomon longed for God's watchful eyes on the temple always, a picture of how God keeps His eyes on His people day and night."},
{q:"Where did Solomon say God dwells when He hears prayer?", options:["In heaven","In the temple only","In Jerusalem","In the ark"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:21",verse:"Hearken therefore unto the supplications of thy servant, and of thy people Israel, which they shall make toward this place: hear thou from thy dwelling place, even from heaven; and when thou hearest, forgive.", insight:"Though the temple stood in Jerusalem, Solomon knew God's true dwelling was heaven, and from there He hears every prayer lifted toward Him."},
{q:"When an oath was taken in the temple over a wrong between neighbors, what did Solomon ask God to do?", options:["Hear from heaven, judge, and repay the wicked while justifying the righteous","Strike both men with a plague","Send the priests to decide the case","Forgive them both without judgment"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:23",verse:"Then hear thou from heaven, and do, and judge thy servants, by requiting the wicked, by recompensing his way upon his own head; and by justifying the righteous, by giving him according to his righteousness.", insight:"Solomon trusted God's perfect judgment over human courts, asking Him to sort the guilty from the innocent when men could not."},
{q:"If Israel were defeated by their enemies and then turned and prayed toward the temple, what would God do?", options:["Hear from heaven, forgive their sin, and bring them back to the land","Give them stronger armies","Send fire on their enemies at once","Scatter them among the nations"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:25",verse:"Then hear thou from the heavens, and forgive the sin of thy people Israel, and bring them again unto the land which thou gavest to them and to their fathers.", insight:"Defeat was not the end for Israel. The road back was always the same: turn, pray, and God would hear, forgive, and restore."},
{q:"When heaven was shut up and there was no rain, what did Solomon pray God would do?", options:["Hear from heaven, forgive their sin, and send rain upon the land","Fill the cisterns by a miracle","Bring clouds from Egypt","Give them manna instead of rain"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:27",verse:"Then hear thou from heaven, and forgive the sin of thy servants, and of thy people Israel, when thou hast taught them the good way, wherein they should walk; and send rain upon thy land, which thou hast given unto thy people for an inheritance.", insight:"Drought was a call to prayer, not despair. Solomon believed God could open the closed heavens when His people humbled themselves."},
{q:"If famine or pestilence came on the land, what were the people to do?", options:["Spread forth their hands in the temple and pray","Flee to the cities of refuge","Offer double sacrifices","Wait until the plague passed"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:29",verse:"Then what prayer or what supplication soever shall be made of any man, or of all thy people Israel, when every one shall know his own sore and his own grief, and shall spread forth his hands in this house:", insight:"Every man knew his own plague and grief, Solomon said, and each one could stretch empty hands toward God in that house."},
{q:"Besides Israel, whom did Solomon ask God to hear?", options:["The stranger from a far country who comes to pray toward the house","The kings of the nations","The merchants of Tyre","The captives of war"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:32",verse:"Moreover concerning the stranger, which is not of thy people Israel, but is come from a far country for thy great name’s sake, and thy mighty hand, and thy stretched out arm; if they come and pray in this house;", insight:"God's house was never meant for one nation only. Solomon prayed for the far-off stranger, because God's mercy has always had a wide reach."},
{q:"Why did Solomon want God to answer the stranger's prayer?", options:["That all the people of the earth may know God's name and fear Him","That Israel's fame would spread","That the stranger would bring gifts","That the temple would be filled"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:33",verse:"Then hear thou from the heavens, even from thy dwelling place, and do according to all that the stranger calleth to thee for; that all people of the earth may know thy name, and fear thee, as doth thy people Israel, and may know that this house which I have built is called by thy name.", insight:"Answered prayer was meant to be a witness. When God heard the foreigner, the whole earth would learn His name."},
{q:"When Israel went out to battle and prayed toward the city and the house, what did Solomon ask God to do?", options:["Hear from heaven and maintain their cause","Give them the strength of ten men","Confuse the enemy's horses","Send angels with swords"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:35",verse:"Then hear thou from the heavens their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause.", insight:"Solomon did not pray for Israel's cleverness in war but for God's justice, that He would uphold their cause."},
{q:"If Israel were carried captive and prayed with all their heart toward their land, what would happen?", options:["God would hear from heaven and maintain their cause","They would be forgotten in exile","Their prayers would be too far away","God would wait until they returned"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:38",verse:"If they return to thee with all their heart and with all their soul in the land of their captivity, whither they have carried them captives, and pray toward their land, which thou gavest unto their fathers, and toward the city which thou hast chosen, and toward the house which I have built for thy name:", insight:"Even in a foreign prison, prayer had a direction: toward home, toward the city, toward God. Distance never weakens a turned heart."},
{q:"What did Solomon ask God to be toward the prayer made in the temple?", options:["Let His eyes be open and His ears be attent","Let His anger be turned away","Let His glory fill the court","Let His angels stand guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:40",verse:"Now, my God, let, I beseech thee, thine eyes be open, and let thine ears be attent unto the prayer that is made in this place.", insight:"Open eyes and listening ears: that is the God Solomon prayed to, one who watches over His people and hears them."},
{q:"What did Solomon pray the priests would be clothed with?", options:["Salvation","Fine linen","Blue and purple","Gold and jewels"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:41",verse:"Now therefore arise, O LORD God, into thy resting place, thou, and the ark of thy strength: let thy priests, O LORD God, be clothed with salvation, and let thy saints rejoice in goodness.", insight:"Better than any robe was the clothing Solomon wanted for the priests: salvation itself, worn like a garment."},
{q:"How did Solomon end his great prayer?", options:["Asking God to remember the mercies of David His servant","Blessing all the congregation","Offering a final sacrifice","Singing a psalm of David"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 6:42",verse:"O LORD God, turn not away the face of thine anointed: remember the mercies of David thy servant.", insight:"He closed not with his own achievements but with God's mercies to David, ending where every prayer should end: on God's faithfulness, not ours."}
]},
{n:7, name:"Fire from Heaven", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 7:14",verse:"If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land."}, facts:["Did you know the fire fell from heaven the moment Solomon finished praying, consuming the burnt offering while the glory of the LORD filled the house?","Did you know Solomon offered twenty and two thousand oxen and an hundred and twenty thousand sheep at the dedication, one of the largest sacrifices ever recorded in Israel?","Did you know God's answer to Solomon's prayer came by night? The LORD appeared to him after the feast was over to give the promise of 2 Chronicles 7:14."], questions:[
{q:"What came down from heaven when Solomon finished praying?", options:["Fire that consumed the burnt offering and the sacrifices","A cloud that covered the people","A voice that shook the temple","Lightning that split the altar"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:1",verse:"Now when Solomon had made an end of praying, the fire came down from heaven, and consumed the burnt offering and the sacrifices; and the glory of the LORD filled the house.", insight:"God answered with fire, the sign He had given before, showing His people that this house and this prayer pleased Him."},
{q:"Why could the priests not enter the house of the LORD?", options:["Because the glory of the LORD filled it","Because the fire was still burning","Because Solomon had shut the doors","Because the people crowded the porch"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:2",verse:"And the priests could not enter into the house of the LORD, because the glory of the LORD had filled the LORD’S house.", insight:"God's glory filled the house so completely that even the priests had to wait outside. His presence fills every space it enters."},
{q:"What did the people do when they saw the fire and the glory?", options:["Bowed with their faces to the ground upon the pavement and worshipped","Ran from the court in fear","Shouted for Solomon to come out","Fell silent and wept"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:3",verse:"And when all the children of Israel saw how the fire came down, and the glory of the LORD upon the house, they bowed themselves with their faces to the ground upon the pavement, and worshipped, and praised the LORD, saying, For he is good; for his mercy endureth for ever.", insight:"They did not stand and watch; they fell on their faces. True worship still bends low when God shows Himself."},
{q:"What words did the people speak as they worshipped?", options:["For He is good, for His mercy endureth for ever","Holy, holy, holy is the LORD","Blessed be the name of the LORD","Great is the LORD and greatly to be praised"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:3",verse:"And when all the children of Israel saw how the fire came down, and the glory of the LORD upon the house, they bowed themselves with their faces to the ground upon the pavement, and worshipped, and praised the LORD, saying, For he is good; for his mercy endureth for ever.", insight:"Their song was short and certain: God is good, and His mercy never ends. That is still the whole gospel in a sentence."},
{q:"How many oxen and sheep did Solomon offer at the dedication?", options:["Twenty and two thousand oxen, and an hundred and twenty thousand sheep","Ten thousand oxen and fifty thousand sheep","A thousand oxen and ten thousand sheep","Five hundred oxen and five thousand sheep"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:5",verse:"And king Solomon offered a sacrifice of twenty and two thousand oxen, and an hundred and twenty thousand sheep: so the king and all the people dedicated the house of God.", insight:"The scale of the offering matched the size of the occasion: a whole nation giving thanks at once."},
{q:"What did the Levites hold as the priests waited on their offices?", options:["The instruments of music of the LORD, which David had made","The trumpets of the sanctuary","The cymbals of the temple","The harps of the singers"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:6",verse:"And the priests waited on their offices: the Levites also with instruments of musick of the LORD, which David the king had made to praise the LORD, because his mercy endureth for ever, when David praised by their ministry; and the priests sounded trumpets before them, and all Israel stood.", insight:"David's instruments were still in use a generation later, a reminder that worship built on God's pattern outlives its builders."},
{q:"Why did Solomon offer sacrifices in the middle of the court?", options:["Because the brasen altar was not able to receive them all","Because the priests were too few","Because the people wanted to see","Because the altar was being repaired"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:7",verse:"Moreover Solomon hallowed the middle of the court that was before the house of the LORD: for there he offered burnt offerings, and the fat of the peace offerings, because the brasen altar which Solomon had made was not able to receive the burnt offerings, and the meat offerings, and the fat.", insight:"There were too many offerings for the altar to hold, so he consecrated the very ground. A full heart always finds room to give."},
{q:"How long did Solomon and all Israel keep the feast?", options:["Seven days","Three days","Fourteen days","Forty days"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:8",verse:"Also at the same time Solomon kept the feast seven days, and all Israel with him, a very great congregation, from the entering in of Hamath unto the river of Egypt.", insight:"A full week of feasting with all Israel, from Hamath to the river of Egypt: joy shared is joy doubled."},
{q:"What did Israel hold on the eighth day?", options:["A solemn assembly","A day of fasting","A second sacrifice","A day of silence"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:9",verse:"And in the eighth day they made a solemn assembly: for they kept the dedication of the altar seven days, and the feast seven days.", insight:"After seven days of dedication and seven of feasting, they closed with a solemn assembly, ending the celebration the way it began: before God."},
{q:"On which day did Solomon send the people home to their tents?", options:["The three and twentieth day of the seventh month","The first day of the eighth month","The tenth day of the seventh month","The last day of the feast"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:10",verse:"And on the three and twentieth day of the seventh month he sent the people away into their tents, glad and merry in heart for the goodness that the LORD had shewed unto David, and to Solomon, and to Israel his people.", insight:"They went home glad and merry of heart for all the goodness of the LORD, the mark of worship that truly worked."},
{q:"When did the LORD appear to Solomon, and what did He say about the temple?", options:["By night, saying He had chosen it for a house of sacrifice","In the morning, saying He would fill it with glory","At noon, saying He would dwell in it forever","In a dream, saying He had rejected it"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:12",verse:"And the LORD appeared to Solomon by night, and said unto him, I have heard thy prayer, and have chosen this place to myself for an house of sacrifice.", insight:"God's answer came in the quiet of night, a personal word to the king who had prayed so publicly."},
{q:"Which three judgments did God say He might send on the land?", options:["Shut heaven with no rain, locusts devouring the land, and pestilence among the people","Famine, sword, and captivity","Earthquake, flood, and fire","Darkness, hail, and plagues"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:13",verse:"If I shut up heaven that there be no rain, or if I command the locusts to devour the land, or if I send pestilence among my people;", insight:"God named the very troubles Solomon had prayed about, showing He had heard every word of that long prayer."},
{q:"What four things must God's people do in the promise of 2 Chronicles 7:14?", options:["Humble themselves, pray, seek His face, and turn from their wicked ways","Fast, weep, mourn, and offer sacrifices","Gather, sing, dance, and feast","Build, give, serve, and obey"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:14",verse:"If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land.", insight:"The most famous promise in the chapter starts with humbling, not striving. God heals lands that first bow low."},
{q:"What did God promise about His eyes and ears toward the house of prayer?", options:["Mine eyes shall be open, and mine ears attent unto the prayer made in this place","They shall be closed until the people repent","They watch only the king's palace","They are turned away from this place"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:15",verse:"Now mine eyes shall be open, and mine ears attent unto the prayer that is made in this place.", insight:"His eyes open, His ears attent: God pays close attention to prayers prayed in His house."},
{q:"What did God promise about His eyes and ears in this place?", options:["His eyes shall be open and His ears attent to the prayer made there","His eyes would watch the priests and His ears the singers","His eyes would close in rest and His ears in peace","His eyes would see the sacrifices and His ears the music"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:15",verse:"Now mine eyes shall be open, and mine ears attent unto the prayer that is made in this place.", insight:"God promised a permanent listening post in that house: open eyes, attentive ears, forever."},
{q:"What did God say would be in the house perpetually?", options:["His eyes and His heart","His glory and His fire","His name and His ark","His priests and His singers"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:16",verse:"For now have I chosen and sanctified this house, that my name may be there for ever: and mine eyes and mine heart shall be there perpetually.", insight:"God put His heart in that house, not just His name. He does not visit His people coldly; He loves the place where they meet Him."},
{q:"What covenant promise did God repeat about David's throne?", options:["There shall not fail thee a man to be ruler in Israel","The throne would stand forever without condition","David's sons would rule all nations","The kingdom would never be divided"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:18",verse:"Then will I stablish the throne of thy kingdom, according as I have covenanted with David thy father, saying, There shall not fail thee a man to be ruler in Israel.", insight:"The promise to David stood firm, carried on God's faithfulness even when Solomon's sons would fail."},
{q:"What did God say He would do if Israel forsook Him and served other gods?", options:["Pluck them up by the roots out of the land and cast the house out of His sight","Leave them to their enemies for a little while","Take away the ark but keep the temple","Send them prophets to warn them again"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:20",verse:"Then will I pluck them up by the roots out of my land which I have given them; and this house, which I have sanctified for my name, will I cast out of my sight, and will make it to be a proverb and a byword among all nations.", insight:"Blessing had a condition, and God spoke the warning plainly: the land and the temple were gifts, not guarantees."},
{q:"What would the high house become to everyone who passed by it?", options:["An astonishment","A heap of ruins","A dwelling for strangers","A forgotten memory"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:21",verse:"And this house, which is high, shall be an astonishment to every one that passeth by it; so that he shall say, Why hath the LORD done thus unto this land, and unto this house?", insight:"The grandest building on earth could become a warning sign. Privilege never protects a people from the cost of turning away."},
{q:"What would the nations say was the reason for all this evil upon Israel?", options:["Because they forsook the LORD and laid hold on other gods","Because their kings were weak","Because their enemies were strong","Because the temple was defiled"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 7:22",verse:"And it shall be answered, Because they forsook the LORD God of their fathers, which brought them forth out of the land of Egypt, and laid hold on other gods, and worshipped them, and served them: therefore hath he brought all this evil upon them.", insight:"Even the watching nations would know the truth: Israel's ruin would be a spiritual failure, not a military one."}
]},
{n:8, name:"Solomon's Dominion", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 8:16",verse:"Now all the work of Solomon was prepared unto the day of the foundation of the house of the LORD, and until it was finished. So the house of the LORD was perfected."}, facts:["Did you know it took Solomon twenty years to finish both the house of the LORD and his own royal palace?","Did you know Solomon made no servants of the children of Israel? They were men of war and captains, while the remaining peoples of the land paid tribute.","Did you know Solomon's ships sailed from Eziongeber on the Red Sea all the way to Ophir, bringing back four hundred and fifty talents of gold?"], questions:[
{q:"How many years did Solomon spend building the house of the LORD and his own house?", options:["Twenty","Seven","Thirteen","Forty"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:1",verse:"And it came to pass at the end of twenty years, wherein Solomon had built the house of the LORD, and his own house,", insight:"Twenty years of building, stone by stone. Great works for God are rarely quick."},
{q:"What did Solomon do with the cities Huram had restored to him?", options:["Built them and settled the children of Israel in them","Gave them back to Huram","Turned them into fortresses","Left them in ruins"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:2",verse:"That the cities which Huram had restored to Solomon, Solomon built them, and caused the children of Israel to dwell there.", insight:"Solomon rebuilt what was handed back and filled it with his people, turning restoration into habitation."},
{q:"Against which city did Solomon go up and prevail?", options:["Hamathzobah","Damascus","Rabbah","Tadmor"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:3",verse:"And Solomon went to Hamath-zobah, and prevailed against it.", insight:"The king of peace still had to fight his battles. Even Solomon's golden age had its Hamathzobah."},
{q:"Which city did Solomon build in the wilderness?", options:["Tadmor","Baalath","Gezer","Megiddo"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:4",verse:"And he built Tadmor in the wilderness, and all the store cities, which he built in Hamath.", insight:"He built in the wilderness itself, showing a kingdom so secure it could plant cities where no one lived."},
{q:"How did Solomon fortify Bethhoron the upper and the nether?", options:["With walls, gates, and bars","With towers and ditches","With armies and chariots","With trenches and palisades"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:5",verse:"Also he built Beth-horon the upper, and Beth-horon the nether, fenced cities, with walls, gates, and bars;", insight:"Wisdom builds and wisdom guards. Solomon fortified the roads that enemies would travel."},
{q:"Which three kinds of cities did Solomon build?", options:["Store cities, chariot cities, and cities of horsemen","Walled cities, market cities, and harbor cities","Cities of gold, silver, and bronze","Cities of the priests, Levites, and singers"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:6",verse:"And Baalath, and all the store cities that Solomon had, and all the chariot cities, and the cities of the horsemen, and all that Solomon desired to build in Jerusalem, and in Lebanon, and throughout all the land of his dominion.", insight:"Storehouses for plenty, chariots for strength, horsemen for speed: Solomon organized his kingdom for both peace and war."},
{q:"What did Solomon make the remaining peoples of the land do?", options:["Pay tribute","Serve in the temple","Join the army","Leave the land"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:8",verse:"But of their children, who were left after them in the land, whom the children of Israel consumed not, them did Solomon make to pay tribute until this day.", insight:"The peoples left in the land paid tribute, but Solomon drew a firm line: his own people would not be enslaved."},
{q:"What did Solomon refuse to make of the children of Israel?", options:["Servants for his work","Soldiers for his wars","Officers over the tribute","Builders of the cities"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:9",verse:"But of the children of Israel did Solomon make no servants for his work; but they were men of war, and chief of his captains, and captains of his chariots and horsemen.", insight:"They were men of war and captains, not slaves. Even at the height of his power, Solomon would not enslave his own people."},
{q:"How many were the chief of Solomon's officers who ruled over the people?", options:["Two hundred and fifty","Five hundred","One hundred","Seventy"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:10",verse:"And these were the chief of king Solomon’s officers, even two hundred and fifty, that bare rule over the people.", insight:"Two hundred and fifty chiefs kept order in a vast kingdom, a picture of government with room to breathe."},
{q:"Why did Solomon move Pharaoh's daughter out of the city of David?", options:["Because the places were holy where the ark of the LORD had come","Because the palace was too small","Because she asked for a house of her own","Because the priests complained"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:11",verse:"And Solomon brought up the daughter of Pharaoh out of the city of David unto the house that he had built for her: for he said, My wife shall not dwell in the house of David king of Israel, because the places are holy, whereunto the ark of the LORD hath come.", insight:"Even a king's marriage bowed to holiness. Solomon would not let his own house crowd the ground where the ark had rested."},
{q:"Where did Solomon house Pharaoh's daughter?", options:["In the house he had built for her","In the house of the forest of Lebanon","In the city of David","In a tent by the temple"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:11",verse:"And Solomon brought up the daughter of Pharaoh out of the city of David unto the house that he had built for her: for he said, My wife shall not dwell in the house of David king of Israel, because the places are holy, whereunto the ark of the LORD hath come.", insight:"He built her a house of her own, honoring both his wife and the holiness of the place she left."},
{q:"Where did Solomon offer his burnt offerings to the LORD?", options:["On the altar he had built before the porch","On the brasen scaffold","In the most holy place","On the roof of the temple"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:12",verse:"Then Solomon offered burnt offerings unto the LORD on the altar of the LORD, which he had built before the porch,", insight:"The king himself brought offerings to the altar he had built, leading his people in worship by example."},
{q:"On which three yearly feasts did Solomon offer sacrifices?", options:["The feast of unleavened bread, the feast of weeks, and the feast of tabernacles","Passover, Pentecost, and the Day of Atonement","The new moons, the sabbaths, and the jubilee","The feast of trumpets, the harvest, and the ingathering"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:13",verse:"Even after a certain rate every day, offering according to the commandment of Moses, on the sabbaths, and on the new moons, and on the solemn feasts, three times in the year, even in the feast of unleavened bread, and in the feast of weeks, and in the feast of tabernacles.", insight:"Solomon kept the calendar God gave Moses, three feasts a year without fail. Faithfulness is often just showing up on time."},
{q:"After whose order did Solomon appoint the courses of the priests?", options:["David his father","Moses the lawgiver","Aaron the high priest","Samuel the prophet"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:14",verse:"And he appointed, according to the order of David his father, the courses of the priests to their service, and the Levites to their charges, to praise and minister before the priests, as the duty of every day required: the porters also by their courses at every gate: for so had David the man of God commanded.", insight:"The son honored the father's order. Good patterns in worship are worth keeping across generations."},
{q:"In what did the priests and Levites not depart from the king's commandment?", options:["Concerning any matter or concerning the treasures","Concerning the sacrifices only","Concerning the building of cities","Concerning the tribute of the peoples"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:15",verse:"And they departed not from the commandment of the king unto the priests and Levites concerning any matter, or concerning the treasures.", insight:"They followed the order exactly, even down to the treasures. Faithfulness in small details keeps big ministries honest."},
{q:"How does the chapter describe the finishing of Solomon's work?", options:["So the house of the LORD was perfected","So the kingdom was established forever","So the people rested from war","So the glory departed"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:16",verse:"Now all the work of Solomon was prepared unto the day of the foundation of the house of the LORD, and until it was finished. So the house of the LORD was perfected.", insight:"Perfected: the word for a work done all the way through. Solomon finished what he started."},
{q:"To which seaside cities did Solomon go in the land of Edom?", options:["Eziongeber and Eloth","Joppa and Acco","Tyre and Sidon","Gaza and Ashkelon"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:17",verse:"Then went Solomon to Ezion-geber, and to Eloth, at the sea side in the land of Edom.", insight:"The wise king went down to the sea himself, where ships could carry Israel's trade to the ends of the earth."},
{q:"What did Huram send to Solomon for the voyage to Ophir?", options:["Ships and servants that had knowledge of the sea","Gold and silver from Tyre","Cedars and algum trees","Captains and soldiers"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:18",verse:"And Huram sent him by the hands of his servants ships, and servants that had knowledge of the sea; and they went with the servants of Solomon to Ophir, and took thence four hundred and fifty talents of gold, and brought them to king Solomon.", insight:"Solomon partnered with those who knew the sea, a reminder that wise leaders borrow skill they do not have."},
{q:"How much gold did Solomon's servants bring back from Ophir?", options:["Four hundred and fifty talents","Six hundred talents","One hundred and twenty talents","A thousand talents"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:18",verse:"And Huram sent him by the hands of his servants ships, and servants that had knowledge of the sea; and they went with the servants of Solomon to Ophir, and took thence four hundred and fifty talents of gold, and brought them to king Solomon.", insight:"Four hundred and fifty talents of gold from one voyage: the reward of a king who planned, partnered, and sent his ships out."},
{q:"Besides the store, chariot, and horsemen cities, what else did Solomon build?", options:["All that he desired in Jerusalem, in Lebanon, and throughout his dominion","A navy of ships on the Great Sea","Walls around every border town","A new palace for Pharaoh's daughter"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 8:6",verse:"And Baalath, and all the store cities that Solomon had, and all the chariot cities, and the cities of the horsemen, and all that Solomon desired to build in Jerusalem, and in Lebanon, and throughout all the land of his dominion.", insight:"The chapter lists a king's desires fulfilled, but the coming chapters will ask what those desires cost him."}
]},
{n:9, name:"The Queen of Sheba", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 9:22",verse:"And king Solomon passed all the kings of the earth in riches and wisdom."}, facts:["Did you know six hundred and threescore and six talents of gold came to Solomon in a single year, not counting what the merchants and traders brought?","Did you know the queen of Sheba confessed that not even half of Solomon's wisdom and greatness had been told her?","Did you know Solomon's throne had six steps guarded by twelve lions, and the chapter says there was not the like made in any kingdom?"], questions:[
{q:"Why did the queen of Sheba come to Jerusalem?", options:["To prove Solomon with hard questions","To make a treaty with Israel","To buy cedar from Lebanon","To see the temple Solomon built"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:1",verse:"And when the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon, she came to prove Solomon with hard questions at Jerusalem, with a very great company, and camels that bare spices, and gold in abundance, and precious stones: and when she was come to Solomon, she communed with him of all that was in her heart.", insight:"She came to test him, not to flatter him, and hard questions are often the doorway to real faith."},
{q:"What did the queen of Sheba bring with her?", options:["Camels bearing spices, gold in abundance, and precious stones","Chariots and horsemen for Solomon's army","Wheat and oil for the temple","Servants to learn Solomon's wisdom"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:1",verse:"And when the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon, she came to prove Solomon with hard questions at Jerusalem, with a very great company, and camels that bare spices, and gold in abundance, and precious stones: and when she was come to Solomon, she communed with him of all that was in her heart.", insight:"She came loaded with gifts, but the greatest thing she carried home was a changed heart."},
{q:"What happened when the queen asked Solomon her hard questions?", options:["He told her all her questions, and nothing was hid from him","He asked for time to consider them","He called his wise men to help","He answered only half of them"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:2",verse:"And Solomon told her all her questions: and there was nothing hid from Solomon which he told her not.", insight:"Every question met its answer. God had given Solomon wisdom deep enough for a queen's hardest riddles."},
{q:"What happened to the queen after she saw Solomon's wisdom and house?", options:["There was no more spirit in her","She wept with joy","She fell on her face","She sang a song of praise"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:4",verse:"And the meat of his table, and the sitting of his servants, and the attendance of his ministers, and their apparel; his cupbearers also, and their apparel; and his ascent by which he went up into the house of the LORD; there was no more spirit in her.", insight:"She was left breathless, overwhelmed by what she saw. The reality of God's blessing outshines every report of it."},
{q:"What did the queen say about the report she had heard in her own land?", options:["It was a true report","It was only half true","It was greatly exaggerated","It was hard to believe"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:5",verse:"And she said to the king, It was a true report which I heard in mine own land of thine acts, and of thy wisdom:", insight:"The report was true, she said, and then admitted the truth was even better than the report."},
{q:"How much of Solomon's greatness had the report told her?", options:["Not even the half","Nearly all of it","Only a small part","More than the truth"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:6",verse:"Howbeit I believed not their words, until I came, and mine eyes had seen it: and, behold, the one half of the greatness of thy wisdom was not told me: for thou exceedest the fame that I heard.", insight:"Not half had been told her. God's gifts to Solomon were bigger than fame could carry."},
{q:"Whom did the queen call happy?", options:["Solomon's servants, who stand continually before him and hear his wisdom","The people of Israel in their prosperity","The builders of the temple","The merchants who traded with him"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:7",verse:"Happy are thy men, and happy are these thy servants, which stand continually before thee, and hear thy wisdom.", insight:"She envied the servants, not the king, because standing near wisdom every day is the happiest place of all."},
{q:"Who did the queen say had set Solomon on his throne?", options:["The LORD his God","His father David","The elders of Israel","The people by acclamation"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:8",verse:"Blessed be the LORD thy God, which delighted in thee to set thee on his throne, to be king for the LORD thy God: because thy God loved Israel, to establish them for ever, therefore made he thee king over them, to do judgment and justice.", insight:"A foreign queen blessed Israel's God and named Him as the source of Solomon's throne. Wisdom had preached its own sermon."},
{q:"How much gold did the queen of Sheba give to Solomon?", options:["An hundred and twenty talents","Sixty talents","Two hundred talents","Fifty talents"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:9",verse:"And she gave the king an hundred and twenty talents of gold, and of spices great abundance, and precious stones: neither was there any such spice as the queen of Sheba gave king Solomon.", insight:"Her gift was fit for a king, but Solomon's greater gift to her was the wisdom she carried home."},
{q:"What did the servants of Huram and of Solomon bring from Ophir?", options:["Gold, algum trees, and precious stones","Silver, ivory, and apes","Spices, wine, and oil","Cedar, fir, and algum"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:10",verse:"And the servants also of Huram, and the servants of Solomon, which brought gold from Ophir, brought algum trees and precious stones.", insight:"The same fleet that made Solomon rich brought the rare algum wood that would sing in the temple."},
{q:"What did Solomon make from the algum trees?", options:["Terraces for the house of the LORD and the palace, and harps and psalteries for singers","Doors for the temple and tables for the palace","Altars for the court and chests for the treasury","Ships for the navy and beams for the house"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:11",verse:"And the king made of the algum trees terraces to the house of the LORD, and to the king’s palace, and harps and psalteries for singers: and there were none such seen before in the land of Judah.", insight:"Rare wood became both terraces and instruments: beauty for God's house and music for God's praise."},
{q:"What did Solomon give the queen of Sheba before she returned to her own land?", options:["All her desire, whatsoever she asked","Double the gold she had brought","A treaty of peace","Cities in the Negev"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:12",verse:"And king Solomon gave to the queen of Sheba all her desire, whatsoever she asked, beside that which she had brought unto the king. So she turned, and went away to her own land, she and her servants.", insight:"He gave her all she desired, and she went home to her own land. Generosity marked the meeting from both sides."},
{q:"How much gold came to Solomon in one year?", options:["Six hundred and threescore and six talents","Five hundred talents","A thousand talents","Three hundred talents"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:13",verse:"Now the weight of gold that came to Solomon in one year was six hundred and threescore and six talents of gold;", insight:"The number is staggering on purpose: no king on earth had ever seen wealth like this."},
{q:"How many targets of beaten gold did Solomon make, and how much went to each?", options:["Two hundred targets, six hundred shekels of gold to one target","Three hundred targets, three hundred shekels to each","One hundred targets, a thousand shekels to each","Five hundred targets, five hundred shekels to each"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:15",verse:"And king Solomon made two hundred targets of beaten gold: six hundred shekels of beaten gold went to one target.", insight:"Golden shields hung in the house of the forest of Lebanon, beauty guarding the king's own house."},
{q:"What was Solomon's great throne made of?", options:["Ivory overlaid with pure gold","Cedar overlaid with silver","Algum wood overlaid with bronze","Stone overlaid with gold"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:17",verse:"Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with pure gold.", insight:"Ivory and pure gold for a throne: the seat of justice in Israel glittered with the wealth God had given."},
{q:"How many lions stood on the six steps of Solomon's throne?", options:["Twelve","Six","Two","Twenty-four"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:19",verse:"And twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other upon the six steps. There was not the like made in any kingdom.", insight:"Twelve lions for twelve tribes, and the chapter adds there was not the like made in any kingdom."},
{q:"What was said of silver in the days of Solomon?", options:["It was nothing accounted of","It was rarer than gold","It was used for the temple vessels","It was kept in the treasury"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:20",verse:"And all the drinking vessels of king Solomon were of gold, and all the vessels of the house of the forest of Lebanon were of pure gold: none were of silver; it was not any thing accounted of in the days of Solomon.", insight:"When gold is common, silver counts for nothing. Prosperity beyond measure can make even precious things feel cheap."},
{q:"How often did the ships of Tarshish come, and what did they bring?", options:["Every three years, bringing gold, silver, ivory, apes, and peacocks","Every year, bringing gold and spices","Every seven years, bringing cedar and algum","Every month, bringing grain and wine"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:21",verse:"For the king’s ships went to Tarshish with the servants of Huram: every three years once came the ships of Tarshish bringing gold, and silver, ivory, and apes, and peacocks.", insight:"Apes and peacocks sailed into Israel's harbors: the world was bringing its wonders to Solomon's door."},
{q:"How long did Solomon reign in Jerusalem over all Israel?", options:["Forty years","Twenty years","Thirty-three years","Fifty years"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:30",verse:"And Solomon reigned in Jerusalem over all Israel forty years.", insight:"Forty years of unrivaled glory, a reign like Israel would never see again."},
{q:"Who reigned in Solomon's stead after his death?", options:["Rehoboam his son","Jeroboam the son of Nebat","His brother Nathan","The elders of Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 9:31",verse:"And Solomon slept with his fathers, and he was buried in the city of David his father: and Rehoboam his son reigned in his stead.", insight:"The wisest king left his throne to a son who would lose most of the kingdom, a sober end to a golden chapter."}
]},
{n:10, name:"The Kingdom Divided", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 10:19",verse:"And Israel rebelled against the house of David unto this day."}, facts:["Did you know the kingdom split at Shechem, where Israel had gathered to crown Rehoboam king?","Did you know the Bible says the cause of the split was of God, fulfilling the word He had spoken by Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam?","Did you know Israel's cry, 'What portion have we in David?', echoed an older rebellion led by Sheba in King David's own day?"], questions:[
{q:"Why did Rehoboam go to Shechem?", options:["All Israel had come there to make him king","To build a palace there","To meet Jeroboam in battle","To offer sacrifices"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:1",verse:"And Rehoboam went to Shechem: for to Shechem were all Israel come to make him king.", insight:"Shechem was the crowning place, but the crown he received there would soon be cut in two."},
{q:"Who returned out of Egypt when Rehoboam was about to be made king?", options:["Jeroboam the son of Nebat","Shishak king of Egypt","Hadad the Edomite","Rezon the son of Eliadah"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:2",verse:"And it came to pass, when Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who was in Egypt, whither he had fled from the presence of Solomon the king, heard it, that Jeroboam returned out of Egypt.", insight:"The exile came home at the very moment of crowning, and God had plans for him."},
{q:"Who came with all Israel to speak to Rehoboam?", options:["Jeroboam","The elders of Judah","The priests and Levites","The captains of the army"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:3",verse:"And they sent and called him. So Jeroboam and all Israel came and spake to Rehoboam, saying,", insight:"The people sent for Jeroboam to be their voice, a sign of where their hearts already leaned."},
{q:"What did Israel ask Rehoboam to do?", options:["Ease the grievous servitude and heavy yoke his father had put on them","Lower the taxes on trade","Free the captives of war","Give them the cities of the Levites"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:4",verse:"Thy father made our yoke grievous: now therefore ease thou somewhat the grievous servitude of thy father, and his heavy yoke that he put upon us, and we will serve thee.", insight:"Their request was reasonable: lighten the load. Even good kings can crush their people without meaning to."},
{q:"What did the people promise if Rehoboam eased their burden?", options:["They would serve him","They would pay double tribute","They would build him a palace","They would crown his son"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:4",verse:"Thy father made our yoke grievous: now therefore ease thou somewhat the grievous servitude of thy father, and his heavy yoke that he put upon us, and we will serve thee.", insight:"They offered him everything a king could want: loyal service, if only he would show them mercy."},
{q:"How long did Rehoboam ask the people to wait for his answer?", options:["Three days","Seven days","One day","Forty days"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:5",verse:"And he said unto them, Come again unto me after three days. And the people departed.", insight:"Three days to think, and he spent them asking the wrong people. Time is no help without wisdom."},
{q:"Whose counsel did Rehoboam seek first?", options:["The old men who had stood before Solomon his father","The priests of the temple","The captains of the army","The prophets of the LORD"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:6",verse:"And king Rehoboam took counsel with the old men that had stood before Solomon his father while he yet lived, saying, What counsel give ye me to return answer to this people?", insight:"He started right, asking men who had served his wise father. The tragedy is that he did not finish right."},
{q:"What did the old men advise Rehoboam?", options:["Be kind to the people, please them, and speak good words to them","Tax them more to show strength","Send Jeroboam back to Egypt","Make a covenant with the elders"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:7",verse:"And they spake unto him, saying, If thou be kind to this people, and please them, and speak good words to them, they will be thy servants for ever.", insight:"Their counsel was pure wisdom: serve the people with kindness, and they will serve you forever."},
{q:"Whose counsel did Rehoboam follow instead?", options:["The young men who were brought up with him","The captains of his guard","The merchants of Jerusalem","The elders of Judah"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:8",verse:"But he forsook the counsel which the old men gave him, and took counsel with the young men that were brought up with him, that stood before him.", insight:"He traded seasoned counsel for the applause of his peers, the oldest mistake a young leader makes."},
{q:"What question did Rehoboam put to the young men?", options:["What counsel give ye that we may answer this people?","How shall I strengthen my kingdom?","Who will stand with me?","What tribute shall I demand?"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:9",verse:"And he said unto them, What advice give ye that we may return answer to this people, which have spoken to me, saying, Ease somewhat the yoke that thy father did put upon us?", insight:"He asked the question hoping for the answer he wanted, and flatterers never disappoint."},
{q:"What boast did the young men put in Rehoboam's mouth?", options:["My little finger shall be thicker than my father's loins","My hand is stronger than my father's hand","My wisdom is greater than Solomon's","My kingdom shall stretch to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:10",verse:"And the young men that were brought up with him spake unto him, saying, Thus shalt thou answer the people that spake unto thee, saying, Thy father made our yoke heavy, but make thou it somewhat lighter for us; thus shalt thou say unto them, My little finger shall be thicker than my father’s loins.", insight:"Pride speaks in comparisons. The young men taught the new king to measure himself against his father, and he believed it."},
{q:"With what did the young men say Rehoboam would chastise the people?", options:["Scorpions, where his father had used whips","Swords, where his father had used spears","Prison, where his father had used fines","Exile, where his father had used labor"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:11",verse:"For whereas my father put a heavy yoke upon you, I will put more to your yoke: my father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.", insight:"Whips to scorpions: cruelty promised as strength. A king who threatens his people has already lost them."},
{q:"How did Rehoboam answer the people?", options:["Roughly","Wisely","Kindly","Slowly"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:14",verse:"And answered them after the advice of the young men, saying, My father made your yoke heavy, but I will add thereto: my father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.", insight:"One rough answer broke a kingdom. Words from a throne carry weight, and Rehoboam threw his away."},
{q:"Why did the king not listen to the people?", options:["The cause was of God, to perform His word spoken by Ahijah to Jeroboam","He was too young to understand","The old men had misled him","Jeroboam had bribed the elders"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:15",verse:"So the king hearkened not unto the people: for the cause was of God, that the LORD might perform his word, which he spake by the hand of Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam the son of Nebat.", insight:"Behind the foolish choice stood God's sovereign hand, working out the word He had spoken through Ahijah."},
{q:"What cry did Israel raise when the king would not listen?", options:["What portion have we in David? Every man to your tents, O Israel","We will serve Rehoboam forever","Bring us another king from Judah","Let us return to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:16",verse:"And when all Israel saw that the king would not hearken unto them, the people answered the king, saying, What portion have we in David? and we have none inheritance in the son of Jesse: every man to your tents, O Israel: and now, David, see to thine own house. So all Israel went to their tents.", insight:"The cry of rebellion rang out, and ten tribes walked away from the house of David in a day."},
{q:"What did Israel tell the house of David to do?", options:["See to its own house","Return to Jerusalem","Repent of its pride","Choose another king"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:16",verse:"And when all Israel saw that the king would not hearken unto them, the people answered the king, saying, What portion have we in David? and we have none inheritance in the son of Jesse: every man to your tents, O Israel: and now, David, see to thine own house. So all Israel went to their tents.", insight:"See to thine own house, David: the saddest farewell a kingdom ever spoke to its king."},
{q:"Over whom did Rehoboam still reign after the revolt?", options:["The children of Israel who dwelt in the cities of Judah","The tribe of Benjamin only","The priests and the Levites","The cities of the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:17",verse:"But as for the children of Israel that dwelt in the cities of Judah, Rehoboam reigned over them.", insight:"Judah remained, and those of Israel who lived in Judah's cities. A remnant stayed loyal when the crowd walked away."},
{q:"What happened to Hadoram, who was over the tribute?", options:["The children of Israel stoned him with stones, and he died","He fled to Jerusalem","He joined Jeroboam","He was taken captive"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:18",verse:"Then king Rehoboam sent Hadoram that was over the tribute; and the children of Israel stoned him with stones, that he died. But king Rehoboam made speed to get him up to his chariot, to flee to Jerusalem.", insight:"The king's tax collector died under stones, the people's answer to the threat of scorpions."},
{q:"What did Rehoboam do after Hadoram was stoned?", options:["Made speed to get up to his chariot and flee to Jerusalem","Gathered his army for war","Sent for the old men again","Sued for peace with Jeroboam"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:18",verse:"Then king Rehoboam sent Hadoram that was over the tribute; and the children of Israel stoned him with stones, that he died. But king Rehoboam made speed to get him up to his chariot, to flee to Jerusalem.", insight:"The king who boasted of scorpions ran for his chariot. Pride always flees faster than it fights."},
{q:"How does the chapter end?", options:["So Israel rebelled against the house of David unto this day","So Rehoboam reigned in peace over Judah","So Jeroboam was crowned in Shechem","So the kingdom was reunited"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 10:19",verse:"And Israel rebelled against the house of David unto this day.", insight:"The split that began that day lasted for generations. One harsh answer can echo for centuries."}
]}
]);
